<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baden is a historic region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> on the right bank of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, between the river and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a>, named after the spa town of Baden-Baden. Ruled by margraves of the Zähringen line from the 12th century, it was greatly enlarged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, becoming an electorate in 1803 and a grand duchy in 1806 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlsruhe">Karlsruhe</a> as capital. After 1918 it was a republic, and since 1952 it has been part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baden.jpg" alt="Baden" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Baden-1802-1819.svg: *Baden.png: ziegelbrenner derivative work: Testtube derivative work: Testtube · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baden-1803-1819.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
